      {
        "url": "https://www.moma.org/collection/works/78389",
        "title": "Henri Matisse. The Red Studio. Issy-les-Moulineaux, fall 1911 | MoMA",
        "content": "\"Where I got the color red—to be sure, I just don't know,\" Matisse once remarked. \"I find that all these things . . . only become what they are to me when I see them together with the color red.\" This painting features a small retrospective of Matisse's recent painting, sculpture, and ceramics, displayed in his studio. The artworks appear in color and in detail, while the room's architecture and furnishings are indicated only by negative gaps in the red surface. The composition's central axis [...] Henri Matisse. The Red Studio\nHenri Matisse. The Red Studio\n\n# Henri Matisse\n\nThe Red Studio\n\nIssy-les-Moulineaux, fall 1911\n\nOil on canvas\n\nAudio from the playlist Collection 1880s–1940s\n\n### \n\nFrom MoMA Design Store\n\nHenri Matisse: The Cut-Outs - Hardcover\nHenri Matisse: Meet the Artist!\nWhen Pigasso Met Mootisse (HB)\nModern Art Desserts: Recipes for Cakes, Cookies, Confections, and Frozen Treats Based on Iconic Works of Art\nPoster Matisse: Dance I [...] 2006\n\nA Splash of Color\n\nThis painting shows Henri Matisse’s art studio. It was very important to him. Matisse’s studio wasn’t red, but he liked the way this color connected everything in the painting.\n\nThink about a place that is special to you. How would you paint it?\n\n2025\n\n## Explore more\n\nHenri Matisse\n\n### Henri Matisse",
